cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use modewise in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "modewise: data-adaptive mode decomposition for multichannel signals"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ian Philip
    family-names: Eglin
    affiliation: "Department of Electronic Systems, Norwegian University of Science and Technology (NTNU)"
version: 0.2.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/ipeglin/modewise"
abstract: >-
  A toolbox for data-adaptive analysis of multichannel recordings such as fMRI and EEG: mode
  decompositions (MVMD, VMD, VLMD, the EMD family, wavelet MRA), spectra and time-frequency maps,
  functional connectivity, epochs, regions and cohort permutation statistics, with a Rust core, a
  Python package and a command line for cohort batches.
keywords:
  - mode decomposition
  - MVMD
  - VLMD
  - EMD
  - wavelets
  - functional connectivity
  - fMRI
  - EEG
  - time-frequency analysis
